  "version": "0.1.22-beta",
  "prepared_at_utc": "2026-10-21T09:44:40+00:00",
  "changes": [
    "Fix T5 viewing-depth exception to count only marked flooded tubes with weapons, matching native candidate counting. Draining a selected non-T5 releases its depth veto; flooding it restores restriction. Recheck confirmation. Preserve marks, native readiness and physical levers; retain .21 raised Feuer and MP host toggle, TRC9. Publishing metadata revision: set Manifest steamFileId 3823181610 for the existing Workshop listing; no gameplay source changes."
  ],
  "validation": {
    "compile": "passed",
    "offline": "passed",
    "in_game": "partial",
    "notes": [
      "Full supplied UBOAT/Unity/Harmony reference compilation passed. 217 targeted offline assertions passed: 85 stock/depth, 82 viewing fire/layout, 50 MP scope display. Other prior suites not re-run. Metadata revision: C# Source byte-identical to tested .22 snapshot; both ZIP manifests verified as Workshop ID 3823181610. Latest owner .22 log records Tube V launch verified=True; live result partial with unresolved whole-panel lockout/refresh issues. Existing copyright/license/credits retained."
    ]
  },
  "known_issues": [
    "Owner reports unchecking T5 at depth locks entire viewing panel and prevents rechecking until drain/reflood; flooded non-T5 also blocks whole panel; delayed refresh/half-full graphic remains. This metadata update does not fix gameplay. MP and shallow recovery remain unverified. No new release/tag/Workshop upload. All peers should use .22/TRC9."
  ],
